※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4484

※ A mask says, of each thing it could pick, whether to pick it -- so it has one
※ truth value for each, and its shape is the array's first dimensions, as many
※ of them as it has.  A shape that is neither leaves things it says nothing
※ about, or says something about things that are not there.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let v: u8⟦4⟧ = ⟦1u8, 2u8, 3u8, 4u8⟧
    let want: bool⟦3⟧ = ⟦true, false, true⟧
    let got: u8⟦⟧ = v⟦want⟧
    got⟦0⟧
